{"duration_api_ms":89866,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4d91f7c3-c13d-4b39-acf3-611ebbd705ad","total_cost_usd":0.160544,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15895,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":9696,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5167},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15895,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9696,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15895,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15895},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":9696,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":15895,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.160544,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":5167,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is essentially a one-parameter curve in flight_path_angle at D=3.385 m, bluntness=1.2, cone=70 deg. It runs from gamma=-1.5 (227k W/m2, 417.9 K) to gamma=-3.57 (274.6k W/m2, 391.1 K), where max_g reaches its 12 g limit. The other design variables are pinned by constraints. Mass-fraction margin at D=3.385 is only 1.4e-4. Bluntness above 1.2 or cone below 70 (except about 69.8-69.9) hits the aero-surrogate hull failures. Hypervolume has plateaued at 0.3555 over the last three rounds. The remaining gain is from filling gaps along the front, so I place all 20 points at gamma values not yet evaluated, on the safe D/b/cone.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-948029610632 (gamma -1.5), C-bbe53564e0b7 (-1.95) and C-f32ce283f0ee (-2.2) show flux rising and bondline T falling smoothly with steeper gamma. The gap between -1.5 and -1.95 is the widest in the front.\",\"C-81e40e27ff03 (-3.57, g=11.999) and C-112b974177e0 (-3.572, g=12.001, infeasible) locate the g cap. C-0265d5374015 (-3.5695) is already feasible at the boundary.\",\"C-3b86cbfeed06 and C-7799f09f0eed (b=1.15, 1.10) give slightly higher flux and lower mass margin than b=1.2, so lowering bluntness does not help.\",\"C-2375647d7e43, C-3d41ce848a30, C-dcc9bfd9f503, C-166a3a760ccb, C-bcce2808c9b8 and C-a554636d8035 fail on surrogate extrapolation. Moving D, b or cone off the current corner risks wasting slots.\",\"C-602600f85327 (D=3.2, mass margin 0.106) versus C-948029610632 (D=3.385, margin 1.4e-4) shows mass fraction is very sensitive to D. D cannot be raised, and gamma does not change the mass margin.\"],\"mechanism\":\"This is partly from the data and partly from prior Allen-Eggers-type reasoning. Peak flux rises with sqrt(sin(gamma)) and the heat pulse shortens at steeper gamma, so bondline T falls. Peak g is set mainly by gamma. With D, b and cone at their constraint-limited corner, gamma is the only free trade-off parameter. The front is a smooth convex monotone curve, so interpolating between neighbouring evaluated points gives accurate predictions. Since gamma does not affect mass fraction and the geometry is unchanged, these points should be feasible and not hit geometry or hull failures. The gain is small but positive.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The expected hypervolume gain per point is small, since the front is already densely sampled. Interpolation errors should be about 0.2-0.5% in flux and under 0.3 K in T. The near-limit points at -3.54 and -3.565 depend on max_g, which reads 11.98-11.999 near the cap. I have not explored other regions such as smaller D or lower cone angle, because they are dominated or fall outside the surrogate hull based on the data shown.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-948029610632\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the shallow-gamma end of the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":228300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the widest gap in front coverage at the low-flux end.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-948029610632\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.5 and -1.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":229500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a front point in an under-sampled region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-948029610632\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.5 and -1.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.65},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":230600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":415.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a front point in an under-sampled region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-948029610632\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.5 and -1.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":231700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":414.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a front point in an under-sampled region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-948029610632\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.7 and -1.95.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":232750,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the gap near C-5a6d2e72f3b4, which is on a slightly different D and cone.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-bbe53564e0b7\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -1.8 and -1.95.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":235600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds coverage on the exact D=3.385, b=1.2, cone=70 geometry.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-bbe53564e0b7\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -1.95 and -2.05.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":237600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a dense front point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-5b7da58ad0af\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -2.05 and -2.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.125},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":240400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a gap in the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-064ad9f5e91d\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -2.2 and -2.35.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.275},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":243800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406.05,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a gap in the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-064ad9f5e91d\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -2.2 and -2.35.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":244400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",